// The verdict — the smallest scene where the rules layer solves the case.
//
// Three suspects. Carol is alibied by placement (aviary all afternoon).
// Bob starts unaccounted, then a witness places him in the aviary at
// 2:30 — a leap: over(0), there at that instant, no invented path.
// Eddie stays unaccounted. Ask the engine who could have done it:
// the ?- goals below consult rules.pl with this scene's fact export
// (open the facts button to read the export; run `npm run serve` —
// the engine loads over HTTP). The answers appear in purple under the
// query results; when exactly one name remains, the line goes bold.
//
// The unknown room is doing the epistemic work: people we can't place
// are parked there, and rules.pl treats "in unknown" as "could be
// anywhere". Alibis shrink the candidate set; the residual is the
// verdict. Delete bob's leap and watch the answer widen to two.

view top
clock 1:00 minute(0.5)
time time_of_death 3:00

room lion_enclosure size(4 2.5 4) door(to aviary)
room aviary size(4 2.5 4) north-of(lion_enclosure)
room unknown size(4 2.5 4) at(-9 0 -9) color(black)

cylinder alice r(0.25) h(1.6) at(lion_enclosure 1 1) color(grey)   // the victim
cylinder carol r(0.25) h(1.6) at(aviary) color(purple)
cylinder eddie r(0.25) h(1.6) at(unknown) color(blue)
cylinder bob r(0.25) h(1.6) at(unknown 1 0) color(red)

set suspects carol eddie bob

// the victim: dead in the lion enclosure at 3:00
at time_of_death
  turn alice to(90 0 0) over(1m) ease(in)
  check in(alice lion_enclosure)
end

// the clue that alibis bob: seen in the aviary at 2:30
walk bob to(aviary 1 0) start(2:30) over(0)
check always in(bob aviary) during(2:30 3:30)   // ...and stays there

// the derivation, as a case file: the eliminations (with each alibi
// named), the remaining candidates, and the verdict
?- cleared(suspects, X, lion_enclosure, time_of_death, Where)
?- could(suspects, X, lion_enclosure, time_of_death)
?- sole(suspects, X, lion_enclosure, time_of_death)
